<!--
  link.xml - copied from TikTok-Unity-SDK_2026-06-09_044640_Callback-deserialization-fix.unitypackage
  (com.tiktok.minigame 1.1.3). Preserves the whole runtime assembly `ttsdk` for
  IL2CPP managed stripping.

  WHY
  TTSDK deserializes native callback payloads with LitJson, which constructs
  the result/model types by reflection (Activator.CreateInstance). The CP's
  mini-game build is IL2CPP + managed stripping. The UnityLinker sees no
  direct `new` for these result types' parameterless constructors and strips
  them, so on a real device Activator.CreateInstance throws:

      System.MissingMethodException: Default constructor not found for type
      TTSDK.TTGetEntranceMissionRewardResult

  GeneralCallbackResult carries [Preserve], but [Preserve] does NOT inherit,
  and its concrete result subclasses (TTGetEntranceMissionRewardResult,
  TTCheckBalanceResult, TTGetLocationSuccessCallbackResult, TTScanCode/
  ShowModal/ShowToast/ShowActionSheet*Result, TTGetShortcutMissionRewardResult)
  are reflection-only - every one is a stripping candidate.

  FIX
  Preserve the whole runtime assembly `ttsdk` so the linker keeps all
  constructors/members in the IL2CPP/WebGL build. Assembly-wide is
  intentional: it also covers nested DTOs and result types added by future
  SDK versions.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="ttsdk" preserve="all"/>
</linker>
